Description: libqcomtee: add libcbor fallback for CBOR support
 The qcomtee library currently relies on QCBOR as its primary CBOR
 implementation. However, QCBOR is not available in several Linux
 distributions, which complicates building, packaging, and deploying
 qcomtee on those platforms.

 This change adds a fallback implementation based on libcbor when
 QCBOR is unavailable. Libcbor is a widely adopted, standards-compliant
 CBOR library implementing RFC 8949 (formerly RFC 7049) and RFC 8742,
 and is readily available on most major distributions, including
 Debian/Ubuntu and Fedora/Red Hat.

 While libcbor is more feature-rich than QCBOR, it is less opinionated
 for embedded use-cases and places greater responsibility on the
 caller for correct memory management and adherence to canonical encoding
 requirements. This fallback implementation includes the necessary handling
 to ensure correct and interoperable CBOR generation within qcomtee.
 By supporting libcbor as a fallback, qcomtee becomes easier to build and
 use across a broader range of environments without sacrificing CBOR
 compatibility.

